WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:05.810
The new Game of Thrones prequel show has begun
with House of the Dragon Episode 1.

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:12.220
It has a tournament, a horrific childbirth,
a secret prophecy, lots of dragons, and Matt

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:13.360
Smith’s butt.

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:17.369
So what does it all mean, and how does the
show compare to the book?

00:00:17.369 --> 00:00:22.810
This video has no spoilers beyond Episode
1 and the original Game of Thrones show.

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:27.070
The episode’s called The Heirs of the Dragon,
because that’s the name of the chapter in

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:29.890
the book the show’s based on, Fire &amp; Blood.

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:35.310
The big question this episode is succession
– who will inherit the Throne?

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:40.240
It starts with a flashback to the Council
at Harrenhal in the year 101.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:44.570
This is two hundred years before Game of Thrones,
and Daenerys and Jon Snow.

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:50.560
And it’s one hundred years after Aegon Targaryen
conquered Westeros and started the Targaryen

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:51.560
dynasty.

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:57.010
At this time, the king is Jaehaerys Targaryen
– he was the fourth king of Westeros, and

00:00:57.010 --> 00:00:59.670
he’s seen as one of the best kings ever.

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:04.900
His reign was peaceful and prosperous, he
reformed laws, and built roads.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:10.120
But Jaehaerys had bad relationships with some
of the women in his life – the book says

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:13.340
“He was better with roads than with daughters”.

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:18.830
And Jaehaerys had a messy succession, deciding
who would rule Westeros after him.

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:24.620
Cause originally Jaehaerys’ heir was his
eldest son Aemon – but Aemon got killed.

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:30.490
So then Jaehaerys said his second son Baelon
was his heir – even though Aemon had a daughter

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:35.650
called Rhaenys – and some people said Rhaenys
or her children should inherit the Throne.

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:40.260
But Jaehaerys chose Baelon, and then Baelon
died of a.. sore tummy.

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:45.170
So then Jaehaerys was like shit, now what
– and he held this big council to choose

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:47.350
the new heir to the Throne.

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:51.750
They held the council at Harrenhal because
it’s the biggest castle in Westeros.

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:56.640
It’s also mostly ruined because Aegon the
Conqueror burned it with his dragon Balerion

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:58.370
a hundred years ago.

00:01:58.370 --> 00:02:02.200
We see Arya at Harrenhal in Game of Thrones
Season 2.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:07.210
So the lords are here to choose an heir, and
the main candidates are Rhaenys Targaryen,

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:11.900
daughter of Aemon, and Viserys Targaryen,
son of Baelon.

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:17.090
In the book, Rhaenys’ son Laenor is a more
popular candidate than Rhaenys, because he’s

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:20.720
male, and the lords prefer male rulers to
women.

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:26.320
Laenor’s claim is supported by his father,
Corlys Velaryon, who’s very rich and influential.

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:32.130
And there are some other candidates – the
book mentions Jaehaerys’ son Vaegon, but

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:37.060
he’s a.. nerd who.. no one likes, and is
a maester sworn to the Citadel.

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:41.780
They also mention Jaehaerys’ daughter Saera,
but she’s busy running a brothel in the

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:42.800
east.

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:48.370
One of Saera’s bastard sons turns up, with
an elephant, but the lords aren’t impressed.

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:53.900
They consider Laenor, and Rhaenys, but in
the end they choose Viserys to be the next

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:59.290
king, because he’s an adult male who inherits
through the male line.

00:02:59.290 --> 00:03:04.510
Many lords see this as an “iron precedent”
the Throne will always be inherited by men

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:09.240
not women – to the great frustration of
Rhaenys and her family.

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:14.580
The books say that Viserys won this vote by
twenty to one, though the maesters who counted

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:19.740
the votes never revealed the numbers – so
some fans speculate that the maesters rigged

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:23.170
the vote to choose the heir they wanted.

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:27.709
Some characters in the books say that the
maesters have a conspiracy against dragons.

00:03:27.709 --> 00:03:33.180
And while Laenor has the dragon Seasmoke,
and Rhaenys rides the dragon Meleys, Viserys

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:37.100
doesn’t ride a dragon, because his dragon
Balerion died.

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:42.100
So maybe the maesters rigged the vote for
Viserys because they preferred a king who

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:45.890
didn’t have a dragon – but.. that’s
just a theory.

00:03:45.890 --> 00:03:48.890
Point is, Viserys becomes heir to the Throne.

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:51.620
And the episode continues about ten years
later.

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:53.099
Viserys is now king.

00:03:53.099 --> 00:03:58.160
And we see his daughter, Princess Rhaenyra,
flying her dragon Syrax.

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:03.980
She parks her dragon at the Dragonpit, which
is like a big stable where the dragons live.

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:09.110
We see the Dragonpit in Game of Thrones two
hundred years later, when it’s become a

00:04:09.110 --> 00:04:10.110
ruin.

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:13.170
The Dragonpit is guarded by the Dragonkeepers.

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:17.739
The books describe them as “proud warriors”,
in gleaming scaled armor”.

00:04:17.739 --> 00:04:23.660
But in Hot D, they’re a “monk-like order”
in grimy robes – maybe scooping dragon poop

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:25.460
is part of their job.

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:30.660
This one seems to have a dragonglass dagger,
which is interesting – dragonglass is a

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:34.470
special volcanic material that can kill white
walkers.

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:40.880
The Dragonkeepers command dragons in the Valyrian
language, which came from Valyria, the ancient

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:43.580
lost empire of the original dragonlords.

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:48.100
Rhaenyra’s dragon Syrax is named after a
Valyrian goddess.

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:52.250
So Rhaenyra puts her dragon in day care, and
we meet Harrold Westerling.

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:57.310
He’s a member of the Kingsguard, and the
sworn protector of Princess Rhaenyra.

00:04:57.310 --> 00:05:02.630
The Targaryen royal family live in the Red
Keep, and we see the Keep full of lords and

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:08.490
courtiers in rich and colourful clothing – this
is the political centre of the realm in a

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:11.440
time of prosperity and splendour.

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:17.120
This courtyard is the place where Cersei Lannister
paints a map of Westeros, two hundred years

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:18.320
later.

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:23.340
Rhaenyra visits her mother, Aemma Arryn, the
wife and queen of King Viserys.

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:28.120
Aemma’s mother was a Targaryen, so she and
Viserys are also cousins.

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:33.030
Aemma doesn’t like it when Rhaenyra goes
flying, like in Game of Thrones when Catelyn

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:35.560
doesn’t like it when Bran goes climbing.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:40.820
Aemma is pregnant, and she tells Rhaenyra
it’s the duty of a lady to make babies for

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:41.820
the realm.

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:45.620
But Rhaenyra says she’d rather be a knight
and ride in battle.

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:50.520
It’s like in Game of Thrones, when Arya
doesn’t want to marry and have kids.

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:56.510
So while Aemma seems resigned to her role
in the patriarchy, Rhaenyra dreams of a different

00:05:56.510 --> 00:05:57.680
life.

00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:01.960
Rhaenyra serves as cupbearer on King Viserys’
small council.

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:05.040
His councillors are Otto Hightower, Hand of
the King.

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:06.970
Lyonel Strong, master of laws.

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:08.669
Mellos, the Grand Maester.

00:06:08.669 --> 00:06:10.870
Lyman Beesbury, master of coin.

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:13.729
And Corlys Velaryon, master of ships.

00:06:13.729 --> 00:06:17.680
&gt;Though at this point in the book, Corlys
had quit the council because he was angry

00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:23.060
about his wife Rhaenys and son Laenor not
getting the Throne at the Harrenhal council.

00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:27.419
Each councillor has a round stone to represent
their presence.

00:06:27.419 --> 00:06:31.229
We also see Ryam Redwyne, the Commander of
the Kingsguard.

00:06:31.229 --> 00:06:36.850
Ryam has been on the Kingsguard for some fifty
years, and he’s a legendary knight.

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:42.530
At one point, King Jaehaerys made Ryam the
Hand of the King – but Ryam was a terrible

00:06:42.530 --> 00:06:47.170
Hand, so Jaehaerys had fire him – turns
out that being a good knight doesn’t make

00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:49.050
you a good politician.

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:52.450
Corlys warns the council about the Triarchy.

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:57.800
The Triarchy is an alliance of the eastern
cities of Tyrosh, Myr and Lys.

00:06:57.800 --> 00:07:02.970
They’ve started attacking pirates on the
Stepstones, these little islands between Westeros

00:07:02.970 --> 00:07:03.970
and Essos.

00:07:03.970 --> 00:07:08.350
And Corlys is worried that if the Triarchy
take control of the Stepstones, they could

00:07:08.350 --> 00:07:11.090
disrupt trade up the narrow sea.

00:07:11.090 --> 00:07:15.810
Corlys’ family the Velaryons are based on
Driftmark in the narrow sea, and they make

00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:17.949
their money off this trade.

00:07:17.949 --> 00:07:23.270
So, like all good prequels, this show might
start with a trade dispute.

00:07:23.270 --> 00:07:27.330
But the other councillors don’t care about
the Stepstones, and they discuss the upcoming

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:30.330
tournament and Queen Aemma’s pregnancy.

00:07:30.330 --> 00:07:35.800
We see Viserys eating an egg, which is a symbol
of fertility and birth.

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:42.800
Though the way Viserys cracks the egg open
is an omen of how Aemma’s pregnancy ends.

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:45.240
Rhaenyra sees her uncle, Prince Daemon.

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:52.229
Daemon sits on the Throne, which he’s not
meant to do, showing his desire for power

00:07:52.229 --> 00:07:54.500
and willingness to break rules.

00:07:54.500 --> 00:08:00.040
Daemon and Rhaenyra speak in Valyrian, and
he gives her a necklace of Valyrian steel

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:04.180
– the special magic steel that was made
in old Valyria.

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:08.450
Just like Daemon has a sword of Valyrian steel,
called Dark Sister.

00:08:08.450 --> 00:08:12.820
Apparently, Daemon’s helmet is also made
of Valyrian steel.

00:08:12.820 --> 00:08:17.820
So the Targaryens in this time celebrate their
Valyrian ancestry – despite the fact that

00:08:17.820 --> 00:08:23.949
the Valyrians were pretty evil – their empire
killed and enslaved thousands of people – yet

00:08:23.949 --> 00:08:26.800
the Targaryens see them as role models.

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:30.699
Rhaenyra hangs out with her friend Alicent
Hightower.

00:08:30.699 --> 00:08:36.800
Alicent wants to study like a proper lady,
but Rhaenyra wants adventure and.. cake.

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:42.559
Alicent and Rhaenyra are kinda like ladylike
Sansa and rebellious Arya – except instead

00:08:42.559 --> 00:08:46.339
of being rivals, Alicent and Rhaenyra are
close friends.

00:08:46.339 --> 00:08:52.040
They talk about Nymeria, a warrior queen from
the east who lived a thousand years ago.

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:58.040
Nymeria led her people on a great migration
and found a new homeland in Dorne – Nymeria

00:08:58.040 --> 00:09:01.939
left a legacy in Dorne of female power and
equality.

00:09:01.939 --> 00:09:06.829
&gt;HBO has worked on a potential spin-off show
about Nymeria.

00:09:06.829 --> 00:09:11.559
Despite Rhaenyra’s rebellious attitude,
she does know all about Nymeria – showing

00:09:11.559 --> 00:09:15.869
that she’s smart, and she’s aware of a
great female leader.

00:09:15.869 --> 00:09:21.139
Which again is like Arya – Arya named her
direwolf after Nymeria.

00:09:21.139 --> 00:09:23.269
We see a weirwood tree in the Red Keep.

00:09:23.269 --> 00:09:30.649
Weirwoods, with their red leaves and carved
faces, are the sacred trees of the old gods,

00:09:30.649 --> 00:09:34.709
the magic power than Bran connects to in Game
of Thrones.

00:09:34.709 --> 00:09:38.829
In the books, there is no weirwood in the
Red Keep – most weirwoods were destroyed

00:09:38.829 --> 00:09:42.470
in the south when the new religion of the
Seven took over.

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:47.829
So this is an interesting change – will
the magic of the old gods have a role in this

00:09:47.829 --> 00:09:48.829
story?

00:09:48.829 --> 00:09:53.990
King Viserys has cuts on his body that he
got from sitting the Iron Throne.

00:09:53.990 --> 00:09:59.399
The Throne is made of sharp swords making
it impossible to sit on comfortably – and

00:09:59.399 --> 00:10:04.939
Aegon the Conqueror made it that way deliberately
– this dangerous throne symbolises that

00:10:04.939 --> 00:10:11.559
kings must use power carefully and wisely,
or else their power will destroy them.

00:10:11.559 --> 00:10:16.440
When a king is cut by the Iron Throne, that
hints that the king isn’t handling power

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:17.440
well.

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:23.019
The Mad King Aerys the Second, the father
of Daenerys, cuts himself on the Throne so

00:10:23.019 --> 00:10:26.379
often that he’s called King Scab.

00:10:26.379 --> 00:10:32.160
King Maegor the Cruel died on the Throne,
and some say he was killed by the Throne.

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:35.670
As though the Throne rejects unworthy kings.

00:10:35.670 --> 00:10:42.259
So it’s very ominous that the Throne cuts
Viserys, and that the wound is not healing.

00:10:42.259 --> 00:10:45.819
Viserys visits his pregnant wife Aemma.

00:10:45.819 --> 00:10:51.480
Aemma jokes that she might hatch a dragon,
which is interesting, because several Targaryens

00:10:51.480 --> 00:10:56.209
in the books give birth to deformed babies
with dragon-like features.

00:10:56.209 --> 00:11:01.489
Daenerys gives birth to a stillborn that is
“scaled like a lizard”, with leathery

00:11:01.489 --> 00:11:02.489
wings.

00:11:02.489 --> 00:11:08.360
The reason for this might be that the Targaryens
have the blood of the dragon – their Valyrian

00:11:08.360 --> 00:11:14.369
ancestors claimed that they were literally
descended from dragons, with like dragon DNA,

00:11:14.369 --> 00:11:17.879
which is probably what allows them to control
dragons.

00:11:17.879 --> 00:11:21.410
Aemma is having a bad time with her pregnancy.

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:25.269
She’s already had multiple stillbirths and
miscarriages.

00:11:25.269 --> 00:11:30.819
The book says Aemma and Viserys first had
sex when she was just thirteen, and some maesters

00:11:30.819 --> 00:11:34.519
say she got pregnant too young, and this damaged
her health.

00:11:34.519 --> 00:11:39.769
But Viserys keeps wanting more kids cause
he wants a son to inherit his Throne.

00:11:39.769 --> 00:11:45.730
Viserys is convinced that their unborn child
is male, because he had a dream of a son,

00:11:45.730 --> 00:11:49.239
and Targaryens do have prophetic dreams of
the future.

00:11:49.239 --> 00:11:55.589
The whole political stability of Westeros
depends on queens producing male heirs, so

00:11:55.589 --> 00:12:01.620
Aemma is reluctantly dragged along with her
husband’s dream – though she says she

00:12:01.620 --> 00:12:03.529
can’t do this again.

00:12:03.529 --> 00:12:10.139
Viserys’ brother, Daemon, is the Commander
of the gold cloaks, the City Watch of King’s

00:12:10.139 --> 00:12:11.139
Landing.

00:12:11.139 --> 00:12:16.319
And he leads a brutal, violent crackdown on..
alleged criminals in the city.

00:12:16.319 --> 00:12:20.569
We see Daemon personally kill a murderer.

00:12:20.569 --> 00:12:26.779
The book says that Daemon delights in mutilating
criminals, cutting off hands and noses and

00:12:26.779 --> 00:12:32.579
cocks – so this is not just about.. law
enforcement, it’s about Viserys enjoying

00:12:32.579 --> 00:12:36.449
violence, spreading fear, and asserting his
power.

00:12:36.449 --> 00:12:42.800
The gold cloaks are like his personal loyal
army, two thousand strong, in the heart of

00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:43.800
the realm.

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:47.670
Otto Hightower, is angry about this bloodbath.

00:12:47.670 --> 00:12:51.750
He wants to reduce Daemon’s power, and prevent
him getting the Throne.

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:57.889
Daemon responds like a smirking sulky teenager,
who’s acting out for attention.

00:12:57.889 --> 00:13:03.120
He misbehaves because he wants his brother
Viserys to notice him and accept him.

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:09.879
Daemon has sex with his lover, Mysaria, but
Daemon can’t climax – he feels unsatisfied,

00:13:09.879 --> 00:13:13.120
with pent up feelings that he can’t seem
to let out.

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:18.110
It’s like the only ways Daemon knows how
to feel better is through sex and violence,

00:13:18.110 --> 00:13:21.059
and if that doesn’t work for him, what will?

00:13:21.059 --> 00:13:26.290
Mysaria suggests that Daemon have sex with
a silver-haired maiden – which is interesting

00:13:26.290 --> 00:13:33.300
because Daemon’s niece Rhaenyra is a silver-haired
maiden, who he seemed pretty close with earlier.

00:13:33.300 --> 00:13:39.230
Daemon is stressed because if Aemma gives
birth to a son, that son will replace Daemon

00:13:39.230 --> 00:13:40.869
as heir to the Throne.

00:13:40.869 --> 00:13:46.179
Viserys holds a big tournament to celebrate
the coming birth of his child.

00:13:46.179 --> 00:13:50.660
There’s jousting, and fighting, and there’s
politics.

00:13:50.660 --> 00:13:56.480
Lord Boremund Baratheon competes – he’s
an ancestor of Robert, Stannis and Renly Baratheon.

00:13:56.480 --> 00:14:01.699
Boremund is also the uncle of Rhaenys Targaryen,
and at the Harrenhal council he supported

00:14:01.699 --> 00:14:04.660
Rhaenys and Laenor in their claim for the
Throne.

00:14:04.660 --> 00:14:08.699
So now, Boremund calls Rhaenys “The Queen
Who Never Was”.

00:14:08.699 --> 00:14:15.779
It’s a little treasonous to publicly undermine
King Viserys by bringing up Rhaenys’ claim,

00:14:15.779 --> 00:14:20.609
but Viserys is chill and he allows the light
treason.

00:14:20.609 --> 00:14:25.850
Prince Daemon joins the tourney, and he chooses
to joust against Gwayne Hightower, the son

00:14:25.850 --> 00:14:29.480
of Otto Hightower, specifically to piss off
Otto.

00:14:29.480 --> 00:14:32.949
He also requests the favour of Otto’s daughter
Alicent.

00:14:32.949 --> 00:14:37.939
So Daemon really is a master of annoying Otto.

00:14:37.939 --> 00:14:42.299
Some of the knights start killing each other
on the tourney grounds, which you’re not

00:14:42.299 --> 00:14:47.170
meant to do, but it does happen – like in
Game of Thrones, when the Mountain attacks

00:14:47.170 --> 00:14:48.999
Loras and the Hound.

00:14:48.999 --> 00:14:54.019
Rhaenys says these knights are “green as
summer grass” – they’re young, dumb

00:14:54.019 --> 00:14:58.480
and full of cum, and have never experienced
real war, or hard times.

00:14:58.480 --> 00:15:03.610
It’s similar to a bit in the books, when
Catelyn says that winter is coming for these

00:15:03.610 --> 00:15:05.109
knights of summer.

00:15:05.109 --> 00:15:12.449
This is about loss of innocence, disillusionment,
the inevitable end of good times.

00:15:12.449 --> 00:15:16.220
The surprise favourite of the tournament is
Criston Cole.

00:15:16.220 --> 00:15:19.269
Criston isn’t from some rich and famous
family.

00:15:19.269 --> 00:15:24.589
He’s the son of a steward, and in Hot D
he’s Dornish – which is interesting, because

00:15:24.589 --> 00:15:28.639
in this time period, Dorne has not yet been
conquered by the Targaryens.

00:15:28.639 --> 00:15:33.100
It’s still an independent kingdom with its
own laws and culture.

00:15:33.100 --> 00:15:39.100
So Criston is an outsider and an underdog,
and he has a lot to gain by proving himself

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:41.290
with his fighting skills.

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:46.959
Criston defeats the famous Prince Daemon in
jousting and combat – partly by attacking

00:15:46.959 --> 00:15:48.660
Daemon while he wasn’t looking.

00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:54.019
Though to be fair, Daemon also played dirty
by tripping Gwayne Hightower horse’s with

00:15:54.019 --> 00:15:57.359
his lance – everyone’s breaking the rules
here.

00:15:57.359 --> 00:16:02.459
But Criston wins, and he clearly makes an
impression on Rhaenyra and Alicent.

00:16:02.459 --> 00:16:06.060
Meanwhile, Queen Aemma’s childbirth goes
wrong.

00:16:06.060 --> 00:16:11.019
Mellos says that Aemma’s gonna die, and
the only way to save the baby is to cut it

00:16:11.019 --> 00:16:15.610
out of her, like a medieval c-section, which
will kill Aemma.

00:16:15.610 --> 00:16:21.799
Viserys is horrified, but he wants his male
heir, so he agrees to cut up his wife open

00:16:21.799 --> 00:16:23.379
to save his child.

00:16:23.379 --> 00:16:24.379
They..

00:16:24.379 --> 00:16:26.730
don’t ask Aemma what she wants.

00:16:26.730 --> 00:16:32.459
So they start the bloody procedure, and it’s
intercut with knights fighting at the tourney

00:16:32.459 --> 00:16:38.329
– the battlefield of men and the birthing
bed of women as two sides in an endless violent

00:16:38.329 --> 00:16:40.949
cycle of death and life.

00:16:40.949 --> 00:16:47.279
Aemma dies, and Viserys gets his baby son,
and names him Baelon, but then Baelon dies

00:16:47.279 --> 00:16:50.170
too, from birth complications maybe.

00:16:50.170 --> 00:16:55.709
So at the funeral, the baby Baelon is cremated
along with Queen Aemma.

00:16:55.709 --> 00:17:01.029
In the books, Aemma just dies in childbirth,
it doesn’t mention a c-section.

00:17:01.029 --> 00:17:05.660
But that does happen to a different character
in the book, Alyssa Velaryon.

00:17:05.660 --> 00:17:11.620
Alyssa was the mother of King Jaehaerys, and
of Boremund Baratheon by her second husband,

00:17:11.620 --> 00:17:12.620
Rogar.

00:17:12.620 --> 00:17:17.220
Rogar kept getting Alyssa pregnant even though
she was too old and it was dangerous for her.

00:17:17.220 --> 00:17:23.640
Her next childbirth went bad, and like Viserys,
Rogar chose to cut his wife open to save the

00:17:23.640 --> 00:17:26.360
baby, because he wanted a son.

00:17:26.360 --> 00:17:30.040
Alyssa’s daughter Rhaena was furious at
Rogar for this.

00:17:30.040 --> 00:17:33.950
She blamed him for Alyssa’s death because
he got her pregnant when it was dangerous

00:17:33.950 --> 00:17:39.900
for her, and she’s angry that he valued
his wife’s life less than he valued making

00:17:39.900 --> 00:17:40.920
a son.

00:17:40.920 --> 00:17:47.210
We can see a hint of that anger on Rhaenyra’s
face, when she looks at Viserys and then says

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:49.190
dracarys – fire.

00:17:49.190 --> 00:17:55.040
Cause this episode highlights how much Rhaenyra
cares for her mother, and how frustrated she

00:17:55.040 --> 00:18:01.020
is that Viserys seems to care more about getting
a son than he cares about his wife and daughter.

00:18:01.020 --> 00:18:06.930
Rhaenyra sees Aemma dead because of Viserys’
dream, and she resents being pushed into the

00:18:06.930 --> 00:18:10.670
same gender role that killed her mother.

00:18:10.670 --> 00:18:13.430
After the funeral, the council talks succession.

00:18:13.430 --> 00:18:18.500
It’s very dangerous when there’s no clear
heir to the Throne, because competing claims

00:18:18.500 --> 00:18:20.850
often lead to war.

00:18:20.850 --> 00:18:26.470
Precedent says Viserys’ brother Daemon is
next in line, but most folks don’t want

00:18:26.470 --> 00:18:29.470
the violent Daemon on the Throne.

00:18:29.470 --> 00:18:35.020
Otto suggests Rhaenyra, and Corlys suggests
Rhaenys, but Lyonel argues there’s never

00:18:35.020 --> 00:18:36.730
been a female ruler.

00:18:36.730 --> 00:18:41.630
So Viserys storms off, leaving the future
of the realm uncertain.

00:18:41.630 --> 00:18:44.070
Otto decides to act.

00:18:44.070 --> 00:18:49.610
He tells his daughter Alicent to put on her
mother’s dress and go “comfort” the

00:18:49.610 --> 00:18:53.030
newly single King Viserys in his bedchamber.

00:18:53.030 --> 00:19:00.380
Otto is similar to Tywin Lannister in Game
of Thrones – being Hand, writing letters,

00:19:00.380 --> 00:19:04.480
using his children for his political ambitions.

00:19:04.480 --> 00:19:12.110
Alicent finds Viserys working on a model city,
using a nerdy hobby to cope with his grief.

00:19:12.110 --> 00:19:18.220
The city looks similar to Dragonstone, but
bigger – it might represent old Valyria.

00:19:18.220 --> 00:19:23.290
Or maybe Viserys is imagining a grand expansion
to the Dragonstone castle.

00:19:23.290 --> 00:19:30.130
There was once another Targaryen king who
dreamed of a white city – the Mad King Aerys.

00:19:30.130 --> 00:19:33.840
Some fans have also noticed that the model
city looks like the opening sequence to Game

00:19:33.840 --> 00:19:34.930
of Thrones.

00:19:34.930 --> 00:19:41.990
Meanwhile, Daemon has his own way of coping
with emotions – he drinks alone, fully clothed,

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:45.410
in the middle of an orgy he set up for his
gold cloaks.

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:51.310
Mysaria prompts him to speak, and Daemon gives
a toast to Viserys’ dead baby – calling

00:19:51.310 --> 00:19:57.100
him the “heir for a day”, celebrating
that with Baelon’s death, Daemon remains

00:19:57.100 --> 00:19:58.510
heir to the Throne.

00:19:58.510 --> 00:20:05.670
Otto tells Viserys this, so Viserys confronts
Daemon, turning his grief for his wife and

00:20:05.670 --> 00:20:08.420
child into fury at his brother.

00:20:08.420 --> 00:20:12.310
Daemon gets angry back, calls Viserys weak.

00:20:12.310 --> 00:20:17.810
So Viserys finally decides to disinherit Daemon,
and sends him away to the Vale.

00:20:17.810 --> 00:20:24.250
It’s tragic that these two brothers, who
love each other, fight when they so need each

00:20:24.250 --> 00:20:25.280
others’ support.

00:20:25.280 --> 00:20:31.380
Immediately after, Viserys again cuts himself
on the Throne – another dark omen.

00:20:31.380 --> 00:20:37.210
So Viserys and Daemon are separated, and that
was probably Otto’s plan, this is why he

00:20:37.210 --> 00:20:39.790
told Viserys about Daemon’s toast.

00:20:39.790 --> 00:20:46.730
Daemon says that Otto is an ambitious scheming
cunt, and Otto himself said that all men want

00:20:46.730 --> 00:20:48.850
“absolute power”.

00:20:48.850 --> 00:20:55.160
At the same time that Otto pushes Daemon away,
he moves his daughter Alicent closer to the

00:20:55.160 --> 00:20:56.160
king.

00:20:56.160 --> 00:21:00.760
Viserys decides to make his daughter Rhaenyra
heir to the Throne.

00:21:00.760 --> 00:21:06.850
He says he was wrong to focus on an unborn
son when Rhaenyra has the potential to be

00:21:06.850 --> 00:21:08.600
a great ruler.

00:21:08.600 --> 00:21:13.050
&gt;Though Viserys knows that the Throne is a
terrible responsibility.

00:21:13.050 --> 00:21:19.390
He knows the danger of dragons and their power
– he talks about Valyria, how their power

00:21:19.390 --> 00:21:21.840
and pride led to their downfall.

00:21:21.840 --> 00:21:26.330
&gt;Though the exact cause of the Doom of Valyria
is a mystery.

00:21:26.330 --> 00:21:29.730
And Viserys tells Rhaenyra a big secret.

00:21:29.730 --> 00:21:34.800
So, a hundred years ago, Aegon Targaryen,
the Conqueror, took over Westeros and started

00:21:34.800 --> 00:21:36.760
the line of Targaryen kings.

00:21:36.760 --> 00:21:43.730
Viserys says that part of why Aegon conquered
Westeros is because he had a dream of a winter

00:21:43.730 --> 00:21:50.470
from the north that would destroy humanity
– Aegon had a dream of the white walkers.

00:21:50.470 --> 00:21:55.760
Aegon believed that a Targaryen king must
unite the realm to save the world from the

00:21:55.760 --> 00:21:59.820
walkers, and that’s why he conquered Westeros.

00:21:59.820 --> 00:22:03.070
This dream of Aegon’s isn’t in the books.

00:22:03.070 --> 00:22:07.550
But it was author George Martin’s idea to
add this to the show, and in the books there

00:22:07.550 --> 00:22:13.170
are other Targaryens who know about a prophecy
to save the world – Aemon, Jaehaerys the

00:22:13.170 --> 00:22:14.740
Second, probably Bloodraven.

00:22:14.740 --> 00:22:21.100
And Rhaegar Targaryen, the brother of Daenerys
and the father of Jon Snow.

00:22:21.100 --> 00:22:26.230
The books say that when Rhaegar was young,
he found something in some scrolls that convinced

00:22:26.230 --> 00:22:28.560
him to be a warrior.

00:22:28.560 --> 00:22:31.910
Maybe Rhaegar discovered Aegon’s white walker
dream.

00:22:31.910 --> 00:22:37.270
Daenerys has a vision of Rhaegar, where Rhaegar
mentions “the song of ice and fire”.

00:22:37.270 --> 00:22:41.830
And Viserys says that Aegon’s dream is called
“The Song of Ice and Fire”.

00:22:41.830 --> 00:22:46.710
This prophecy is probably why Rhaegar ran
off with Lyanna and had Jon Snow – he musta

00:22:46.710 --> 00:22:51.840
believed that his son would stop the white
walkers, finally fulfilling Aegon’s dream

00:22:51.840 --> 00:22:54.980
of the Targaryens saving the world.

00:22:54.980 --> 00:22:59.620
Of course, we know this dream doesn’t exactly
come true.

00:22:59.620 --> 00:23:05.330
In Game of Thrones Season 8, the white walkers
are not defeated by a Targaryen or by a united

00:23:05.330 --> 00:23:11.270
Westeros – Arya Stark kills the white walkers,
and at the time, Westeros is divided, with

00:23:11.270 --> 00:23:13.570
Cersei Lannister on the Throne.

00:23:13.570 --> 00:23:17.090
So maybe this dream was misinterpreted.

00:23:17.090 --> 00:23:22.150
Aegon was right about the white walkers – but
he was wrong to think that his family would

00:23:22.150 --> 00:23:23.310
be the saviours.

00:23:23.310 --> 00:23:27.750
It’s like how Viserys misinterprets his
dream about his heir.

00:23:27.750 --> 00:23:32.180
He was right that there’d be thundering
hooves and splintering shields, and his heir

00:23:32.180 --> 00:23:33.180
on the Throne.

00:23:33.180 --> 00:23:36.820
But he was wrong to assume that his heir was
a son.

00:23:36.820 --> 00:23:41.520
In the books, prophecies and dreams are often
misinterpreted due to characters’ ambition

00:23:41.520 --> 00:23:45.950
and biases, often leading to their downfall.

00:23:45.950 --> 00:23:50.960
As Marwyn says, “Prophecy will bite your
prick off every time”.

00:23:50.960 --> 00:23:55.220
Viserys wears this Valyrian steel dagger.

00:23:55.220 --> 00:23:59.870
This is the same dagger that Arya uses to
kill the Night King in Game of Thrones.

00:23:59.870 --> 00:24:03.090
The same dagger she uses to kill Littlefinger.

00:24:03.090 --> 00:24:05.930
The same dagger in this book Sam found.

00:24:05.930 --> 00:24:10.830
The same dagger that an assassin used against
Catelyn, and that Littlefinger lied about

00:24:10.830 --> 00:24:13.950
to start the whole war in GOT Season 1.

00:24:13.950 --> 00:24:17.790
So is this special dagger part of the prophecy?

00:24:17.790 --> 00:24:22.350
Or is it just some.. cosmic coincidence that
this is the knife that saves the world?

00:24:22.350 --> 00:24:23.350
[This knife isn’t super important in the
books].

00:24:23.350 --> 00:24:28.500
The showrunners say they included this prophecy
and this knife to raise the stakes in Hot

00:24:28.500 --> 00:24:31.940
D, and to connect it with the conflict in
Game of Thrones.

00:24:31.940 --> 00:24:37.430
Viserys tells Rhaenyra to promise him to keep
this secret dream.

00:24:37.430 --> 00:24:42.660
Just like Ned Stark promises Lyanna to keep
the secret of Jon Snow.

00:24:42.660 --> 00:24:48.490
There’s a big ceremony where the lords of
the realm swear loyalty to Rhaenyra, and promise

00:24:48.490 --> 00:24:52.330
to support her claim to the Throne when Viserys
dies.

00:24:52.330 --> 00:24:57.100
She is set to become the first female ruler
of Westeros.

00:24:57.100 --> 00:25:02.060
But this moment isn’t all.. triumphant – it
feels dangerous.

00:25:02.060 --> 00:25:04.870
Daemon is angry that he’s been replaced.

00:25:04.870 --> 00:25:08.100
Rhaenys and her family have been snubbed again.

00:25:08.100 --> 00:25:10.090
Otto is plotting.

00:25:10.090 --> 00:25:15.480
Some of these lords don’t look happy about
a female heir, this does go against the precedent

00:25:15.480 --> 00:25:17.320
of the Harrenhal Council.

00:25:17.320 --> 00:25:23.780
And Rhaenyra never wanted any of this, all
she wanted was to fly and have fun and eat

00:25:23.780 --> 00:25:24.780
cake.

00:25:24.780 --> 00:25:30.210
But now she not only has to rule the continent,
she has to save it from the frosty apocalypse

00:25:30.210 --> 00:25:33.480
cause her great-great-great-grandpa had a
dream.

00:25:33.480 --> 00:25:39.310
All the power and dreams of House Targaryen
weigh upon her, and the theme of this episode

00:25:39.310 --> 00:25:43.230
is that power and dreams are dangerous.

00:25:43.230 --> 00:25:49.340
House of the Dragon is based on the book Fire
&amp; Blood – Season 1 covers Chapter 12, Heirs

00:25:49.340 --> 00:25:50.440
